  "description": "PEBKEM crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H104 La6 N22 O30 4+,4(N1 O3 1-),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La3 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La3D (La) has 6 O neighbors; La1D (La) has 6 O neighbors; La2D (La) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.996-4.621 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.23-151.28°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [La3L3(OH)2(NO3)4]·7H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
